"The prognosis is influenced by several documented factors. The preoperative PSA was elevated at 10. The surgical findings include a Gleason 4+3 with tertiary pattern 5 (ISUP grade group 3), positive surgical margins, seminal vesicle invasion, and documented lymph node metastasis. The biopsy showed a Gleason 3+4 (ISUP grade group 2). The presence of lymph node metastasis and positive margins are concerning factors driving the risk. Countervailing findings include the absence of lymphovascular invasion and the absence of intraductal carcinoma on biopsy. Missing postoperative PSA or follow-up data significantly widens the uncertainty regarding the subsequent trajectory. Information regarding postoperative PSA levels and its subsequent trend is crucial for refining this prognosis. The current heuristic horizon suggests a potential recurrence within a range of months. The fixed estimated horizon is 42.57 months. This is a predicted recurrence horizon, not evidence of observed recurrence. The sensitivity range is 31.93–53.21 months; its coverage has not been validated."
